___TESTS___

scenarios:
- name: Default fields load the bare SDK URL and scope the denied default to 32 regions
  code: |-
    const mockData = {
        siteId: 'default',
        theme: 'light',
        apiEndpoint: '',
        heading: '',
        message: '',
        adsDataRedaction: false,
        urlPassthrough: false
    };

    let defaults = [];
    mock('setDefaultConsentState', function(state) {
        defaults.push(state);
    });

    let injectedUrl = null;
    mock('injectScript', function(url, onSuccess, onFailure) {
        injectedUrl = url;
        onSuccess();
    });

    mock('gtagSet', function() {
        fail('gtagSet must not be called when both flags are off');
    });

    runCode(mockData);

    assertApi('gtmOnSuccess').wasCalled();
    assertThat(injectedUrl).isEqualTo('https://veloconsent.com/v1/velo.js');
    assertThat(defaults.length).isEqualTo(1);
    assertThat(defaults[0].ad_storage).isEqualTo('denied');
    assertThat(defaults[0].analytics_storage).isEqualTo('denied');
    assertThat(defaults[0].security_storage).isEqualTo('granted');
    assertThat(defaults[0].region.length).isEqualTo(32);
    assertThat(defaults[0].wait_for_update).isEqualTo(500);
- name: Site, theme and API endpoint travel as encoded query parameters
  code: |-
    const mockData = {
        siteId: 'acme',
        theme: 'dark',
        apiEndpoint: 'https://app.veloconsent.com',
        heading: '',
        message: '',
        adsDataRedaction: false,
        urlPassthrough: false
    };

    mock('setDefaultConsentState', function() {});

    let injectedUrl = null;
    mock('injectScript', function(url, onSuccess, onFailure) {
        injectedUrl = url;
        onSuccess();
    });

    runCode(mockData);

    assertApi('gtmOnSuccess').wasCalled();
    assertThat(injectedUrl).isEqualTo(
        'https://veloconsent.com/v1/velo.js?site=acme&theme=dark&api=https%3A%2F%2Fapp.veloconsent.com'
    );
- name: Redaction and URL passthrough flags reach gtagSet
  code: |-
    const mockData = {
        siteId: 'default',
        theme: 'light',
        apiEndpoint: '',
        heading: '',
        message: '',
        adsDataRedaction: true,
        urlPassthrough: true
    };

    mock('setDefaultConsentState', function() {});
    mock('injectScript', function(url, onSuccess, onFailure) {
        onSuccess();
    });

    let gtagSetCalls = [];
    mock('gtagSet', function(key, value) {
        gtagSetCalls.push([key, value]);
    });

    runCode(mockData);

    assertApi('gtmOnSuccess').wasCalled();
    assertThat(gtagSetCalls).isEqualTo([['ads_data_redaction', true], ['url_passthrough', true]]);
- name: A failed SDK load fails the tag
  code: |-
    const mockData = {
        siteId: 'default',
        theme: 'light',
        apiEndpoint: '',
        heading: '',
        message: '',
        adsDataRedaction: false,
        urlPassthrough: false
    };

    mock('setDefaultConsentState', function() {});
    mock('injectScript', function(url, onSuccess, onFailure) {
        onFailure();
    });

    runCode(mockData);

    assertApi('gtmOnFailure').wasCalled();
    assertApi('gtmOnSuccess').wasNotCalled();


___NOTES___

Created for Velo (a product of Amplio Data). One tag installs the whole CMP:
it sets a region-scoped Google Consent Mode v2 default synchronously (EEA +
UK + Switzerland denied until the visitor decides; rest of world follows
Velo's opt-out model), then injects the Velo SDK (velo.js), which renders the
banner, resolves regional policy, applies Global Privacy Control, sends
gtag consent updates on every decision, and pushes a `velo_consent_update`
event (with a `velo_categories` object) to the data layer for trigger use.

Fire this tag on the Consent Initialization - All Pages trigger.

Configuration transport: GTM's sandboxed injectScript(url) cannot set data-*
attributes on the script element it creates, so this template passes site,
theme, API endpoint and text overrides as query parameters on velo.js's own
src. The SDK reads its src query string as a first-class config channel
(banner-sdk/src/config.js srcQueryConfig); data-* attributes win over query
parameters when both are present.

Versioning: keep OPT_IN_REGIONS in this file's sandboxed JS in lockstep with
packages/banner-sdk/src/payload.js's list of the same name. They cannot share
a real import (GTM's sandbox has no module loader), so this is a deliberate,
commented duplicate — any change to the SDK's region list needs a matching
change here, and vice versa.

This template replaces the earlier "Velo – Consent Mode Bridge" template and
the Custom HTML installation it depended on: the SDK now pushes its decision
to the data layer itself, so no bridge snippet exists anymore.

Submitted to the public Community Template Gallery (Google's review + listing
process at https://tagmanager.google.com/gallery) from this repository.
Importing and using it privately in any GTM container (Templates -> New ->
Import) also works with no further steps.
